{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_frontend_review", "label": "Frontend review \u2014 2026-08-05", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L1-L470", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_swallowed_error_class", "label": "The swallowed-Supabase-error defect class", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L368-L378", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`const { data } = await supabase...` is valid TypeScript, passes tsc, eslint and every test, and silently converts an infrastructure failure into a confident wrong user-facing claim. Six of eight commits in this review were the same defect; the repo had already been bitten by the empty-vs-failed collapse twice. Every gate green while the thing is broken."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_no_restricted_syntax_lint_rule", "label": "Option A \u2014 no-restricted-syntax esquery lint rule", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L379-L399", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ivan chose A; shipped in ~8 lines of eslint.config.mjs, no custom plugin \u2014 esquery supports :has()/:not(). The subject is the rightmost compound so the error points at `{ data }`; the await is matched with :has(AwaitExpression) so it still catches the `as` cast form. Chosen because it fails at author time, matching the repo's 'make the wrong thing impossible' posture (grant-level revokes, 42501 negative tests)."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_decision_1_check_in_method_ambiguity", "label": "Decision 1 \u2014 check_in_method cannot distinguish tap from staff scan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L232-L284", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PREMISE REJECTED by Ivan 2026-08-06. The section was written from the code that CONSUMED check_in_method without reading the code that PRODUCED it \u2014 the exact failure CLAUDE.md rule 14 was added for one day earlier, second occurrence in two days. The real defect was that self-serve was built as a tap, not a scan."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_decision_3_ruled_out_pipeline_moves", "label": "Decision 3 \u2014 pipeline recommendations recorded but ruled out", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L296-L314", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "high-end-visual-design wanted a warmer ground + secondary accent (ruled out \u2014 the exact move that produced the 4.55:1 \u2192 4.23:1 WCAG failure); gpt-taste wanted a display face (ruled out \u2014 locked, and adds a webfont the stack avoids); emilkowalski-motion wanted roster-row motion (not done \u2014 a live door surface needs a deliberate call and a prefers-reduced-motion path). No two skills deadlocked, so no forced 3-option choice."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_agenda_read_failure_as_deleted_agenda", "label": "A failed agenda read rendered as a deleted agenda (2ad5f09)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L85-L98", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_load_failure_as_empty_state", "label": "Load failures rendered as 'nothing here' (54cfa83, c20b2ad)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L99-L126", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verified by revoking SELECT on agenda_blocks from anon and staff roles rather than trusting the code path. generateMetadata's swallow left deliberate under an eslint-disable naming the reason: throwing would replace a working page with an error boundary over a link preview."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_self_scan_mislabelling", "label": "Every QR check-in reported as a 'self-scan' (c739e32)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L127-L143", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_door_button_focus_ring", "label": "Door check-in button had no visible focus ring (7bc7f59)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L144-L161", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_demo_fixture_rot", "label": "Demo fixture rot + over-promising banner (5530764)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L188-L200", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The unused `checkinOpen` eslint warning was a genuine bug, not noise: the variable existed because the banner was supposed to respect publication and didn't."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_gate_numbers_measured", "label": "Final gate numbers \u2014 measured, not assumed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L318-L340", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "530 passed / 165 skipped, next build clean at 22 route entries (not the documented 21 \u2014 already stale before this run), eslint 0 err + 5 warn. Two corrections to the brief's baseline, both verified by diffing the reviewer's own pre-change run. pnpm test:rls was NOT run."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_concurrent_session_worktree_edits", "label": "Another session editing the same worktree during review", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L341-L364", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four cron files appeared modified after the final gate run. Left completely alone \u2014 not committed, stashed or reverted \u2014 because handoff_04082026 \u00a72 records that uncommitted worktree changes with no commits behind them are how work was nearly destroyed before. Combined tree measured 533/167; 530/165 is the figure for this session's changes alone."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_text_scale_correction", "label": "Text-scale claim corrected by measurement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L209-L216", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The '190 arbitrary text-[Npx]' finding was a stale doc repeated. Measured: 1 arbitrary value (in /poster, a fixed-size print artifact) against 193 calc(Npx*var(--text-scale)) uses. The Text-size setting works; the older unfreeze doc is stale."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_frontend_review", "target": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_swallowed_error_class", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_location": "L368", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_no_restricted_syntax_lint_rule", "target": "docs_plans_2026_08_05_frontend_review_swallowed_error_class", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-08-05-frontend-review.md", "source_loca